#exception-box(title: "THE SEVEN FATAL CUET TRAPS")[
  1. *Trap 1 (First Universal Adult Franchise Election):* The first territory in India to hold an election under universal adult franchise was *Manipur in June 1948*, NOT the 1951–52 Indian general elections.
  2. *Trap 2 (Operation Polo Target):* Operation Polo was launched against *Hyderabad in September 1948*, NOT against Goa or Kashmir.
  3. *Trap 3 (Kashmir Accession Date):* Maharaja Hari Singh signed the Instrument of Accession on *26 October 1947*, NOT on 15 August 1947.
  4. *Trap 4 (Junagadh Integration Method):* Junagadh was integrated via a *democratic plebiscite in February 1948*, NOT by military conquest or royal decree.
  5. *Trap 5 (Potti Sriramulu's Fast Duration):* Potti Sriramulu fasted for *58 days* before dying on *15 December 1952*, NOT 21 days or 40 days.
  6. *Trap 6 (SRC Composition):* The States Reorganisation Commission (1953) was chaired by *Justice Fazal Ali*, with members *K.M. Panikkar* and *H.N. Kunzru*. Do not confuse with the Dhar Commission or JVP Committee!
  7. *Trap 7 (1956 Act State Count):* The States Reorganisation Act of 1956 created exactly *14 States and 6 Union Territories*, NOT 28 states!
]

